selected_signatures.description:
Generate an image from a text prompt.
You can specify the image size, style, model, and number of images to generate.
You don't need to change default parameters if you don't have any specific requirements.
Recraft has both raster and vector models. Recraft models come in a `_raster` and a `_vector` variant: a raster model (e.g. recraftv4_1_raster) produces a raster image (PNG/WEBP), while a vector model (e.g. recraftv4_1_vector) produces a true SVG vector file. Whenever the user asks for a vector, an SVG, a scalable logo, or an icon, pass the `_vector` variant of the model — that is the reliable way to get an SVG. Use the `_raster` variant for photos and raster artwork. recraftv4_1_flash_raster has no vector variant. See the `model` parameter for the full list of variants.
Besides Recraft models, this tool supports external models such as nano_banana_2, nano_banana_pro, gpt_image_2_medium or bytedance_seedreamv5_pro (see the `model` parameter for the full list); availability depends on your subscription and is validated server-side. External models produce raster images only: they have no `_vector` variants, cannot generate SVG, and do not support custom styles.
Recraft also has a large library of built-in "basic styles" beyond the default models. Call the `list_basic_styles` tool to explore the full variety of available styles, then apply a chosen one via its `input_style_id`.
To apply a basic or custom style, pass its `input_style_id` (see list_basic_styles, list_styles and create_style) and omit `input_style`: the image type is taken from the style.
URLs to generated images, their previews in WEBP format as base64 encoded bytes and the credits the call used will be returned in the response.


Recraft accounts: every user has a personal account and may be a member of team workspaces. Exactly one account is active for this MCP connection at a time. The personal account is active unless the user selected a workspace with select_workspace; that choice holds across sessions and conversations until the user changes it or selects "personal". get_user lists the personal account and every workspace the user is a member of, with its workspace_id, role, plan and available credits, and marks the active one. When the user names a team, brand, client or workspace, call get_user to find it and confirm with the user before calling select_workspace; never select a workspace on your own.
Billing: a call in the personal account is charged to the personal balance. A call in a workspace is charged to the user's seat subscription in that workspace first, then to the workspace credit account, never to the personal balance; its results are stored in the workspace where teammates see them, and the workspace's shared styles are available. When the active account has no credits for a call, the call fails and nothing is charged anywhere; the error names the active account and, if another of the user's accounts has more credits, says which one (JFYI); a workspace is topped up by a billing admin at https://www.recraft.ai/profile/workspace. The Design Agent (call_agent) always runs in the personal account.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__recraft__generate_image(args: {
  // Output aspect ratio, such as "1:1", "16:9" or "3:4". Pixel dimensions are chosen by the model. Required for variate_image. If omitted, image_edit follows the first input image; generation defaults to 1:1.
  image_size?: "1:1" | "2:1" | "1:2" | "3:2" | "2:3" | "4:3" | "3:4" | "5:4" | "4:5" | "6:10" | "14:10" | "10:14" | "16:9" | "9:16";
  // Visual style to apply. Use this parameter only if you want to refine the image generation. Mutually exclusive with input_style_id, you can't specify both of them. If you will provide a style that is not available for the specified model, generation will fail. If omitted, a type compatible with the model is used. Styles use-cases: - realistic_image: for realistic images, photos, portraits, landscapes, etc. Raster is generated. - digital_illustration: for digital illustrations, concept art, fantasy art, etc. Raster is generated. - vector_illustration: for vector illustrations, logos, icons, etc. Vector is generated. - icon: for icons, small graphics (only in recraftv2). Vector is generated. - logo_raster: for graphic design, raster logos, posters, emblems, and badges (only in recraftv3). Raster is generated.
  input_style?: "realistic_image" | "digital_illustration" | "vector_illustration" | "icon" | "logo_raster";
  // ID of a custom style to apply (from list_styles or create_style). Mutually exclusive with input_style, you can't specify both of them. The image type is taken from the style automatically; omit model to use the model the style was created for.
  input_style_id?: string;
  // Model to use. If omitted, recraftv4_1 is used and picks raster or vector output itself. Recraft models: - recraftv4_1_raster / recraftv4_1_vector: the latest model, use it in most cases. - recraftv4_1_pro_raster / recraftv4_1_pro_vector: the best-quality model, but relatively slow and expensive. - recraftv4_1_flash_raster: the fastest and cheapest v4.1 model, for rapid iteration and high-volume generation when speed matters more than top quality. It has no `_vector` variant and does not support custom styles (input_style_id). - recraftv3_raster / recraftv3_vector: the previous model, supports the most styles (input_style) and custom styles. - recraftv2_raster / recraftv2_vector: the oldest model, it has a bit cheaper generation. When specifying a Recraft model, pass a `_raster` or `_vector` variant: `_raster` produces a raster image (PNG/WEBP), `_vector` produces a true SVG vector file. To generate a vector / SVG / scalable logo or icon, pass a `_vector` variant — this is the reliable way to get an SVG output. External models (availability depends on your subscription and is validated server-side): nano_banana_2, gpt_image_2p5_sunburst, nano_banana_pro, nano_banana_2p1, gpt_image_2_medium, gpt_image_2_low, gpt_image_2_high, nano_banana_pro_4k, nano_banana_2_with_4k, gpt_image_2p5_flare, gemini_25_flash_image, nano_banana_2_lite, bytedance_seedreamv5_pro, grok_imagine_image_2, gpt_image_1p5_low, flux1_kontext_pro, flux1_kontext_max, flux2_pro, gpt_image_1_high, gpt_image_1_medium, bytedance-seedreamv4, qwen_image. External models have no `_vector` variants, cannot generate SVG / vector output, and do not support custom styles (input_style_id) or input_style.
  model?: "recraftv4_1_raster" | "recraftv4_1_vector" | "recraftv4_1_pro_raster" | "recraftv4_1_pro_vector" | "recraftv4_1_flash_raster" | "recraftv3_raster" | "recraftv3_vector" | "recraftv2_raster" | "recraftv2_vector" | "nano_banana_2" | "gpt_image_2p5_sunburst" | "nano_banana_pro" | "nano_banana_2p1" | "gpt_image_2_medium" | "gpt_image_2_low" | "gpt_image_2_high" | "nano_banana_pro_4k" | "nano_banana_2_with_4k" | "gpt_image_2p5_flare" | "gemini_25_flash_image" | "nano_banana_2_lite" | "bytedance_seedreamv5_pro" | "grok_imagine_image_2" | "gpt_image_1p5_low" | "flux1_kontext_pro" | "flux1_kontext_max" | "flux2_pro" | "gpt_image_1_high" | "gpt_image_1_medium" | "bytedance-seedreamv4" | "qwen_image";
  // Number of images to generate. Should be from 1 to 6. Default is 1.
  n?: number;
  // Text prompt of the image you want to generate. Its length should be from 1 to 10000 characters.
  prompt: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
